{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run/agent-source && sed -n '225,248p' raft.go\"","aggregated_output":"\n\t\t\t// Heartbeat failed! Transition to the candidate state\n\t\t\tlastLeaderAddr, lastLeaderID := r.LeaderWithID()\n\t\t\tr.setLeader(\"\", \"\")\n\n\t\t\tif r.configurations.latestIndex == 0 {\n\t\t\t\tif !didWarn {\n\t\t\t\t\tr.logger.Warn(\"no known peers, aborting election\")\n\t\t\t\t\tdidWarn = true\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t} else if r.configurations.latestIndex == r.configurations.committedIndex &&\n\t\t\t\t!hasVote(r.configurations.latest, r.localID) {\n\t\t\t\tif !didWarn {\n\t\t\t\t\tr.logger.Warn(\"not part of stable configuration, aborting election\")\n\t\t\t\t\tdidWarn = true\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tmetrics.IncrCounter([]string{\"raft\", \"transition\", \"heartbeat_timeout\"}, 1)\n\t\t\t\tif hasVote(r.configurations.latest, r.localID) {\n\t\t\t\t\tr.logger.Warn(\"heartbeat timeout reached, starting election\", \"last-leader-addr\", lastLeaderAddr, \"last-leader-id\", lastLeaderID)\n\t\t\t\t\tr.setState(Candidate)\n\t\t\t\t\treturn\n\t\t\t\t} else if !didWarn {\n\t\t\t\t\tr.logger.Warn(\"heartbeat timeout reached, not part of a stable configuration or a non-voter, not triggering a leader election\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nd={\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Interpreted the no-snapshot receipt and closed that child question. Receipt bdf2837a4c004f95b6c9b19db4fb8154 evaluated all four comparisons: after a restart with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs of a node holding no snapshot, the reported configuration is empty (violated twice, as an id list and as a server count of zero), while the same restart without the feature reports {A,B,C} (holds twice). The mechanism is the parent question's scan start combined with the eager replay, and the consequence is stronger than a stale membership: the node comes up with no membership at all. I acquired the election gate that governs what such a node does next and recorded the account, including the two source-derived consequences I did not execute.\\\",\n \\\"sources\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"s-election-gate\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":225,\\\"end_line\\\":246,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}],\n \\\"investigations\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"16929a65990d446dad09fb1f6c9fe1a2-question-0\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"explained\\\"}],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[\n  {\\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"16929a65990d446dad09fb1f6c9fe1a2-question-0\\\",\n   \\\"experiment_id\\\":\\\"16929a65990d446dad09fb1f6c9fe1a2-experiment\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"s-scan\\\",\\\"s-restorecommitted\\\",\\\"s-processlogs\\\",\\\"s-confentry\\\",\\\"s-quorumsize\\\",\\\"s-election-gate\\\",\\\"s-votegrant\\\"],\n   \\\"executions\\\":{\\\"bdf2837a4c004f95b6c9b19db4fb8154\\\":[1,2,0]},\n   \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"violated\\\",\\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The declared predicate is that a node restarted with the feature rebuilds its membership from the configuration entry in its log even when it has no snapshot; the witness contradicts it in both forms. Admission index 0 records the fixture: cluster {A,B,C} with B leading, node A holding zero snapshots, a staged commit index of 11 over a log ending at 12, and A reporting {A,B,C} while running. After A is restarted with Config.RestoreCommittedLogs (event index 1) it returns, replays to index 13, and reports an empty configuration - neither the id list nor the server count matches the bootstrap membership (comparisons 0 and 1 violated). The control restart without the feature (event index 2) reports {A,B,C} with three servers (comparisons 2 and 3 hold). Mechanism: the scan starts at max(lastSnapshotIndex, lastApplied)+1, restoreFromCommittedLogs has already raised lastApplied to the persisted commit index (api.go 724-753, raft.go 1296-1363), and with no snapshot lastSnapshotIndex is zero, so every configuration entry in the log lies below the scan start and processConfigurationLogEntry is never called (api.go 610-620); the FSM replay still consumes those entries as ordinary commits. Consequences derived from source, not executed here: with latestIndex zero the node's heartbeat timeout logs 'no known peers, aborting election' and never transitions to candidate (raft.go 225-246), and its vote handling skips the membership check for an empty configuration, so it grants votes to candidates it does not know (raft.go 1660-1680). Limits: the observation is a construction state with a 300ms settle, in-memory stores with scaled timeouts, a graceful shutdown, and the node held no snapshots because the harness never took one rather than because of a store failure; the election and vote behaviours remain source-derived.\\\",\n   \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"The empty configuration is observed at construction; the node's subsequent refusal to campaign and its vote grants are derived from source, not executed.\\\",\n    \\\"The absence of snapshots is arranged by the harness (ten-minute interval, none taken) rather than caused by a store failure.\\\",\n    \\\"In-memory stores, scaled timeouts and a graceful shutdown; one run per mode.\\\"],\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The identical restart without the feature rebuilds {A,B,C}, so the empty configuration is not a property of the stores or of the restart procedure.\\\",\n    \\\"The node's FSM did replay the log to index 13, so the empty configuration is not explained by missing log entries.\\\"]}]}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
