{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Interpreted the no-snapshot receipt and closed that child question. Receipt bdf2837a4c004f95b6c9b19db4fb8154 evaluated all four comparisons as declared: a node holding zero snapshots, a staged commit index of 11 over a log ending at 12 and reporting {A,B,C} while running came up after a feature-enabled restart with an empty configuration — zero servers, neither the id list nor the count matching the bootstrap membership (both violated, witness index 1) — while the identical restart without the feature reported {A,B,C} with three servers (both holds, index 2). The mechanism is the parent question's scan start combined with the eager replay: with no snapshot the scan begins above every configuration entry, so none is processed, even though the FSM still replays the log to index 13. I acquired the election gate that governs such a node's next step and recorded the account with its two source-derived consequences — with latestIndex zero the node logs no known peers and never becomes a candidate, and its vote handling skips the membership check for an empty configuration so it would grant votes it cannot evaluate — explicitly flagged as derived rather than executed. The child question is marked explained, its limits recorded (construction-state observation with a 300 ms settle, harness-arranged absence of snapshots rather than a store failure, in-memory stores with scaled timeouts, one run per mode), and the counterevidence noted (the control rebuilds the membership, and the FSM replay rules out missing entries as the cause).\"}"}}
